    "title": "Dothan Police Charge Three Local Men With Human Trafficking Following Hotel Investigation - NewsBreak",
    "text": "3 hours ago On December 10, 2025, the Dothan Police Department in Alabama charged Adam Scott Moore (42), Jeremy Leonard Blackmon (39), and Jimmie Lee Covington Jr. (38) with two counts each of human trafficking in the second degree. The charges followed a two-month investigation. Police allege the suspects arranged illegal sexual activities at local hotels and used a social media platform to connect clients with adult women.\nThe investigation began in November as a drug-related inquiry. During the process, police uncovered evidence of additional crimes. Moore is also charged with chemical endangerment of a child. Blackmon faces an additional charge of first-degree rape and has five outstanding failure to appear warrants. All three men are being held without bond at the Houston County Jail.\nAuthorities highlight the importance of addressing human trafficking. They ask anyone with information to contact the Dothan Police Department or Central Alabama Crime Stoppers. The investigation is ongoing, and more arrests or charges may occur. Due to the sensitive nature of the case, no further details have been released.\nVisit here for more details This post includes content assisted by AI tools. Please refer to the source for verification and additional information. Learn more.",
